From 973d76b392dccc6802e3c15dd8000b35c7bbd411 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eivind FRITZEN <eivind.fritzen@cappelendamm.no>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:44:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Mouse buttons and the wheel as bindings, and extra inputs a
 game defines

A keyboard profile binds the mouse's buttons (SDL's numbers) and each way of its wheel like keys: a binding being
scanned for the keyboard takes the next button pressed or notch turned. A wheel binding reads as held for 60 ms a
notch, released 60 ms between two, so a game that reads its controller once a frame sees each notch as a press; at
most 3 wait, and a notch turned while a menu holds the input is the menu's.

EXTRA_1-EXTRA_8 are actions a game defines beyond the N64's buttons (a reload or crouch key, previous and next weapon):
hidden and unbound until a game names and enables one and gives it defaults, read by its patches through
profiles::get_extra_inputs (bit n for EXTRA_<n+1>). A profile saved before has them at their defaults.

GeneralTabOptions takes a game's own default and description for Mouse Sensitivity, for a game played with mouse
look; without them the stock ones (off by default) as before.

On every build: nothing changes for a game that binds no mouse input and enables no extra input.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
